<title>JAPAN: S.Korea's Cheju Island mulling samurais--sources.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Cheju Island mulling samurais--sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheju Island is planning to launch samurai bonds as early as next week, underwriting sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>Cheju Island, a tourist resort, may launch about 20 billion yen worth of samurai bonds with a maturity of 10 years, they said.</p>
<p>One underwriter said that a public Thai petroleum company is also preparing to launch samurais soon.</p>
</text>
